WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 2: Family Time.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:11.020
In this unit, your child learns the words for family
members (mum, dad, sister, brother, grandma, grandpa),

3
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:15.300
some breakfast and fruit words, and how to count from 1 to 10.

4
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:20.180
They talk about who is in their family and
how families help and have fun together.

5
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.380
The gentle idea is that families love and help each other.

6
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:29.000
The goal is warm, confident talking
in English — not perfect spelling.

7
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:35.800
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:42.740
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name the
people in a family (mother, father, sister, brother, grandma,

9
00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:43.800
grandpa, baby).

10
00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:50.600
you will also name some breakfast foods and fruits
(pancakes, cereal, milk, mango, banana, grapes).

11
00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:55.560
you will also count from 1 to 10,
and count backwards from 10 to 1.

12
00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.240
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:04.360
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
mother, mum, father, dad, sister, brother.

14
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.880
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.800
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:19.520
The reading sequence includes Breakfast at
Grandma's House and Talk about Family Time.

17
00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:20.900
Read actively.

18
00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:25.640
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.720
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.240
The first language focus is Language pattern 1.

21
00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:40.440
Listen to the model, point to the matching
picture, then say the pattern: This is my ___.

22
00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:47.220
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

23
00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:51.580
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

24
00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:56.080
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

25
00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:59.860
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

26
00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.300
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

27
00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:04.820
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:11.480
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

29
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.440
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

30
00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:20.300
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
